    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Extract deterministic L2 visual features from local media or prepared image\r\nframes.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input local media path used when --frame is omitted.\r\n          --frame TEXT ...    Display-oriented image frame path. Repeatable.\r\n          --module TEXT:{quality,shot,detect,face,ocr} ... REQUIRED \r\n                              L2 module to execute. Repeatable.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media feature --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --frame /tmp/frame-0001.jpg --module quality --module shot\r\n  $ lyra-cli media feature --input /tmp/photo.jpg --module quality\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - --frame is repeatable and should contain display-oriented extracted images.\r\n  - quality and shot are deterministic Core modules; no prompt or VLM is used.\r\n  - detect, face and ocr are reserved for optional visual Providers.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Extract deterministic L2 visual features from local media or prepared image\r\nframes.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input local media path used when --frame is omitted.\r\n          --frame TEXT ...    Display-oriented image frame path. Repeatable.\r\n          --module TEXT:{quality,shot,detect,face,ocr} ... REQUIRED \r\n                              L2 module to execute. Repeatable.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media feature --input /tmp/clip.mp4 --frame /tmp/frame-0001.jpg --module quality --module shot\r\n  $ lyra-cli media feature --input /tmp/photo.jpg --module quality\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - --frame is repeatable and should contain display-oriented extracted images.\r\n  - quality and shot are deterministic Core modules; no prompt or VLM is used.\r\n  - detect, face and ocr are reserved for optional visual Providers.\r\n",
